{
  "tool": "ruff",
  "provenance": "observed (driven by a Python stdio script, not by the Go adapter; the Go adapter smoke is internal/engine/code_diagnostics_ruff_smoke_test.go)",
  "platform": "darwin/arm64",
  "versions": {
    "ruff": "0.15.20"
  },
  "location": "uv tool install by the user (~/.local/share/uv/tools/ruff/bin/ruff, linked from ~/.local/bin/ruff); wheel RECORD sha256 matches the binary.",
  "sanitization": "Disposable synthetic project in a temp dir replaced with /fixture; stderr log lines omitted; message text kept verbatim (no user content).",
  "argv": [
    "/installed/ruff",
    "server"
  ],
  "env": {
    "HOME": "<empty temp dir>",
    "PATH": "/usr/bin:/bin"
  },
  "cwd": "/fixture (the project root; no workspaceFolders sent)",
  "fixture": {
    "pyproject.toml": "[project]\nname = \"smoke\"\nversion = \"0\"\n\n[tool.ruff]\nextend = \"../outside/ruff.toml\"\n",
    "../outside/ruff.toml": "line-length = 20\n[lint]\nextend-select = [\"E501\"]\n",
    "drafts": {
      "a.py v1": "x = (1\n",
      "a.py v2": "x = 1\n",
      "b.py v1": "s = '😀'; import os\nyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy = 1\n"
    }
  },
  "client": {
    "capabilities": {
      "general": {
        "positionEncodings": [
          "utf-16"
        ]
      }
    },
    "workspaceFolders": null,
    "serverRequests": "none observed"
  },
  "initialize": {
    "serverInfo": {
      "name": "ruff",
      "version": "0.15.20"
    },
    "capabilities": {
      "positionEncoding": "utf-16",
      "textDocumentSync": {
        "change": 2,
        "openClose": true,
        "willSave": false,
        "willSaveWaitUntil": false
      },
      "diagnosticProvider": {
        "identifier": "Ruff",
        "interFileDependencies": false,
        "workDoneProgress": true,
        "workspaceDiagnostics": false
      }
    }
  },
  "shutdown": {
    "result": null,
    "exitCode": 0
  },
  "notes": [
    "Ruff advertises diagnosticProvider (pull) but pushes publishDiagnostics anyway, even to a client that declares neither publishDiagnostics nor pull diagnostics.",
    "Every push carries the document version, so matching results are current and drawn inline.",
    "A file that does not parse reports only invalid-syntax (severity 1); lint findings are severity 2 with string codes, codeDescription and data (fix/noqa edits, which the bridge ignores). Messages may be multi-line.",
    "The fix edit and didClose each produced an empty publication.",
    "E501 at line-length 20 came from the extend target outside the project: configuration outside the root is applied. Only the project's own pyproject.toml/ruff.toml/.ruff.toml are bound into approval.",
    "Without dynamic registration Ruff does not reload configuration on its own; a changed bound config changes the approval fingerprint instead.",
    "No server->client requests; nothing written to the project or HOME; no .ruff_cache.",
    "A non-canonical temp path (/var vs /private/var) made Ruff silently ignore the project config; the adapter launches in the canonical authorized root."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "open-syntax-error",
      "step": "open a.py broken",
      "publications": [
        {
          "params": {
            "diagnostics": [
              {
                "code": "invalid-syntax",
                "message": "unexpected EOF while parsing",
                "range": {
                  "end": {
                    "character": 0,
                    "line": 1
                  },
                  "start": {
                    "character": 0,
                    "line": 1
                  }
                },
                "severity": 1,
                "source": "Ruff",
                "tags": []
              }
            ],
            "uri": "file:///fixture/a.py",
            "version": 1
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fix-clears",
      "step": "change a.py fixed",
      "publications": [
        {
          "params": {
            "diagnostics": [],
            "uri": "file:///fixture/a.py",
            "version": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
